# Protocol — Metric specification ({{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}})

The authoritative definition of the FROZEN primary metric and every co-tracked metric. Fires whenever
you reason about the primary. `docs/charter.md` references this; the scoring math itself lives in
`{{FROZEN_SCORER_PATH}}` (FROZEN).

## Primary metric (FROZEN)
`{{PRIMARY_METRIC}}` = {{METRIC_DEFINITION}}
- **Direction:** {{PRIMARY_DIRECTION}} = better.
- **Hard bounds:** {{METRIC_HARD_BOUNDS}}.
- **Plausible a-priori range:** {{METRIC_PLAUSIBLE_RANGE}}.
- **Computed by:** `{{FROZEN_SCORER_PATH}}`. You change what FEEDS it, never how it is computed.
[[OPTIONAL — metric has theoretical ceilings:
- **Ceilings (hard upper bounds under a fixed forward/model):** {{CEILING_DEFINITIONS}}. A score above
  its own ceiling is impossible → a bug or metric leak.
]]

## Co-tracked metrics (NOT primary)
- **Guardrail:** `{{GUARDRAIL_METRIC}}` — {{GUARDRAIL_USE}}.
- **Diagnostics:** {{DIAGNOSTIC_METRICS}}.
[[OPTIONAL — the primary should always be reported with a subgroup split:
- **Always report the {{SUBGROUP_SPLIT}} split** — a mean propped up by the easy subgroup is not a
  real win.
]]

## Metric validation gate (do once, before trusting any ranking)
{{METRIC_VALIDATION_GATE}}
<!-- e.g. confirm the scorer returns the expected value on a known input, collapses to the no-skill
     floor on a scrambled input, and reproduces the baseline number. If it doesn't, STOP — the metric
     wiring is wrong and every ranking built on it is meaningless. -->

## What may and may not touch the metric
- **Mutable (feeds the metric):** {{METRIC_INPUTS}}.
- **FROZEN (never edit to change a number):** the scoring formula, the data, known ground truth.
